  - [1m[38;5;153mauth.js[39m:[0m new [38;5;153mrequireLoginOrToken[39m middleware. It lets the request through if it has [38;5;153mAuthorization: Bearer [39m
    [38;5;153m$REPORTS_TOKEN[39m, and otherwise falls back to [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m. It uses a constant-time comparison so the token can't be
    guessed from response timing. If [38;5;153mREPORTS_TOKEN[39m isn't set, the token path is off and the route works exactly as
    before.
  - [1m[38;5;153mserver.js[39m:[0m [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m now uses [38;5;153mrequireLoginOrToken[39m.

